99t|a|Wide; extend in breadth, or from side to side; -- opposed to narrow; as, a broad street, a broad table; an inch broad. ; Extending far and wide; extensive; vast; as, the broad expanse of ocean. ; Extended, in the sense of diffused; open; clear; full. ; Fig.: Having a large measure of any thing or quality; not limited; not restrained; -- applied to any subject, and retaining the literal idea more or less clearly, the precise meaning depending largely on the substantive. ; Comprehensive; liberal; enlarged. ; Plain; evident; as, a broad hint. ; Free; unrestrained; unconfined. ; Characterized by breadth. See Breadth. ; Cross; coarse; indelicate; as, a broad compliment; a broad joke; broad humor. ; Strongly marked; as, a broad Scotch accent.	j:ugj,83,7;1o9l,71,6;42k,69,5;lak,61,4;koo,57,6;15n7,56,6;1lx2,56,3;ugm,55,7;hv4,55,11;24pg,55,5;1o19,52,1;1jdr,47,1;406,47,6;1gn8,46,7;9f5,44,6~1o18,15,19;ro1,6,18;b6p,39,15;66p,32,12;hv4,55,11;14n9,9,11;1wk3,34,10;27b0,3,10;1soh,20,10;zfo,8,9;12n7,33,7;1gn8,46,7;4ft,9,7;ugj,83,7;1fh2,25,7	e:1074,63,4;qng,51,4;5sj,48,5;ztf,41,3;1fa0,36,10;18ab,33,3;11gh,28,3;169,27,2;1z60,26,9;im4,26,4;10tq,25,8;p3e,19,6;qod,14,17;1oc5,13,6;12bs,11,2~22p7,4,83;qod,14,17;qw7,6,11;1fa0,36,10;1z60,26,9;1w24,6,9;1p8k,5,8;10tq,25,8;1oc5,13,6;1gns,4,6;p3e,19,6;5sj,48,5;qng,51,4;im4,26,4;1074,63,4
