9fw|a|Not having sensation; senseless; inanimate; unconscious; without intelligence or volition; as, the brute earth; the brute powers of nature. ; Not possessing reason, irrational; unthinking; as, a brute beast; the brute creation. ; Of, pertaining to, or characteristic of, a brute beast. Hence: Brutal; cruel; fierce; ferocious; savage; pitiless; as, brute violence. ; Having the physical powers predominating over the mental; coarse; unpolished; unintelligent. ; Rough; uncivilized; unfeeling.	j:sop,57,113;1yak,31,3~sop,57,113;1yak,31,3
